 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to the consumption of alcohol by students under the age of twenty-one who are enrolled in certain courses of study",
    "basePrintNo": "S6531",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6531-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§65 & 65-c, ABC L",
    "lawSection": "Alcoholic Beverage Control Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6531\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to the\nconsumption of alcohol by students under the age of twenty-one who are\nenrolled in certain courses of study\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nTo allow students, under the age of twenty-one, to taste or sample\nalcoholic beverages in off campus settings as part of a required\ncurriculum.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\n§ 1 amends subdivision 5 of section 65 of the alcoholic beverage\ncontrol law\n\n§ 2 amends paragraph (a) of subdivision 2 of section 65-c of the\nalcoholic beverage control law\n\n§ 3 is the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nWith the growth of the spirit and beverage industry in New York State,\nmany academic institutions have developed or expanded curriculums to\nmeet the growing need for workers in the agriculture, hospitality and\nbeverage industry. Many of these programs and curricula offer hands-on\ntraining to familiarize students with the food or beverages they will\nbe working with.\n\nCurrently, students under the age of twenty-one are not allowed to\npartake in tastings at off campus sites. Given the rise of wineries,\ndistilleries and breweries in the state, many programs are interested\nin bringing their students to these establishments. This bill would\nallow students to gain a better understanding of this growing industry\nthrough direct contact with professionals in the field. The curriculum\nfor these programs are licensed and registered by the State Education\nDepartment. Any consumption would take place under the supervision of\nan instructor and in accordance with the approved curriculum, to\nensure that responsible tastings are conducted.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew Bill\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
